def page(file,title,body):
 (P/file).write_text(f'<!doctype html><html lang="en-AU"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{H(title)} · AIT Unit 3</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../style.css"></head><body><main><nav><a href="index.html">Unit 3 worked evidence</a> · <a href="../../index.html#contents">Textbook contents</a></nav><h1>{H(title)}</h1>{body}</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8')
page('planning-model.html','Festival planning representations', '''<p>Invented model, not actual project progress. These are distinct representations for different planning questions.</p>
<h2>Storyboard: twelve-second introduction</h2><ol><li>0–4 s: festival title over an establishing scene; narration introduces the event.</li><li>4–8 s: approach to venue; narration explains how to find the programme.</li><li>8–12 s: venue label; preserve caption space and end with a readable programme instruction.</li></ol>
<h2>Site map</h2><p>Programme is the parent destination. Printmaking and Photography are child session destinations. Each child provides a labelled return to Programme; the Help control sits beside the task. The reference uses same-page section links, not a server booking system.</p>
<h2>Decision flow</h2><p>Start → Open Programme → Choose a session → Read time and room → Can the visitor use the stated route? If yes: follow the route and finish. If no: use the published help/access contact process, then review an agreed alternative. The class prototype does not submit a request.</p>
<h2>Gantt-style day blocks and dependencies</h2><div style="overflow:auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Model project schedule"><table><caption>Illustrative estimates; separate people available for the two day-2 tasks</caption><thead><tr><th>Task / prerequisite</th><th>D1</th><th>D2</th><th>D3</th><th>D4</th><th>D5</th><th>D6</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Confirm brief / none</th><td>Confirm</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>Prototype / brief</th><td></td><td>Review</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>Assets / brief</th><td></td><td>Prepare</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>Build / prototype + assets</th><td></td><td></td><td>Build</td><td>Build</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>Test / build</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>Test</td><td></td></tr><tr><th>Revise + retest / findings</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>Retest</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Text equivalent:</strong> Confirm on day 1. Two available people review the prototype and prepare assets in parallel on day 2. Build requires both and takes days 3–4. Test on day 5; revise/retest on day 6. If one person must do both day-2 jobs, revise the schedule and dependent dates. Day blocks are illustrative, not additional teaching weeks.</p><p><a href="planning.html#independent">Develop your own brief, drawings and schedule</a></p>''')
